WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.310
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.180
Satoshi continues to fight in
the Pokémon World Championships,

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.200
and is currently ranked 890th.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.870
So far, he’s maintained
a flawless winning streak.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.220
Yamabuki City, Kanto Region

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.380
Seeking his next challenge,
he’s come to Yamabuki City.
Yamabuki City, Kanto Region

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.660
Yes. Its moves are sharp.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:53.750
Aren’t they?

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.090
I feel like we’re totally unstoppable!

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:02.130
Are you sure you should
be boasting so much in the Fighting Dojo?

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:05.750
Our Karate Master is no trifling foe.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.130
Think he’ll battle me?

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.810
He’s battling
someone else right now.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.800
A challenger arrived
before you.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:12.750
Huh?

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.630
Worry not.
He’ll be done shortly.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.770
The Master cannot lose!

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.850
Hey, Go, let’s watch the battle!

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:32.650
It seems you’re still unsure.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.650
Go!

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.240
Oh, Satoshi.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.560
You can’t pick between
Ebiwarar and Sawamurar?

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.050
Should I go with Ebiwarar
and his barrage of focused punches,

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:51.270
or Sawamurar with his
immensely destructive kicks?

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:54.670
Do I really have to pick just one?

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.920
Indeed. That’s the rule.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.100
The Fighting Dojo
can only give trainers...

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.430
...Sawamurar <i>or</i> Ebiwarar.
One or the other.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:06.940
Satoshi, I know!
We’ll get one each!

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.940
Then you can trade for mine!

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.220
Huh?!

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:14.210
A Championships Trainer is nearby.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.990
That must mean...

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.660
...the challenger battling right now.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:21.570
I see!

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.000
PocketMonsters

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.500
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.260
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.760
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.470
And skip the slow send-off

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.850
Be it through fire or through water

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.560
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.480
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:56.650
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:01.450
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.450
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:12.040
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:17.460
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.760
No need to hesitate! Try!

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.010
Let's have a fight!

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.720
1: Once the battle's done

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.060
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:33.190
On 3, let's be friends!

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:38.690
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:43.950
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.490
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:50.750
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.420
I choose you!

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.420
The Terror of Otosupus!!
Saito, the Lone Warrior!

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.930
Let’s go, everyone!

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:09.350
Excuse—

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.560
Satoshi, are you okay?!

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.610
Ebiwarar?!

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.540
I did not anticipate
such power...

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.000
Referee, call it.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.250
O-Of course!

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.140
Otosupus wins!

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:41.010
As such, the winner is Saito!

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.630
Are you okay, Ebiwarar?

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:52.800
Ebiwarar!

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:56.690
You fought well, Ebiwarar.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.800
Return.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.140
I can’t believe it...
Our Karate Master was utterly helpless.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.980
Otosupus is formidable.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:11.080
Its trainer demonstrated an
utterly impeccable fighting technique, too.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.570
Otosupus?

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.580
Return, Otosupus.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:22.030
That was a fine battle.
I thank you.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.430
That’s for the Championships?

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.400
This is an official
battle announcement.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.560
You’re signed up for the Championships?

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.310
Would you like to battle? Or not?

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:42.880
My name is Satoshi.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.070
I’m fighting in the Championships, too.
I’d like to battle you!

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.570
I accept your challenge.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.070
Really? All right!

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.200
Official battle appointment made!

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:00.210
My name is Saito.
I hail from Galar.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.210
Galar?

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.670
May we use this arena?

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:07.240
By all means.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.340
You said your name was Satoshi, yes?

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:14.940
I am the owner of this Fighting Dojo.
They call me the Karate Master.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.350
You may use this place as you see fit.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:20.050
Thank you, Karate Master!

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:21.610
Are you here to battle, too?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:27.220
Oh, no, I heard I could get
Ebiwarar or Sawamurar if I came here.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.230
Indeed you can.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:33.030
That is, if you can defeat me in battle.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.740
I have to battle?!

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:39.290
Well, first let us observe
Lady Saito’s battle.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:43.190
Live alongside Pokémon...
Battle alongside Pokémon...

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.730
One way to do that lies here.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:52.390
Lady Saito is a Gym Leader
in the Galar Region, you see.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.510
A Gym Leader?!

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:59.020
She is known as both
the Fighting-type Gym Leader...

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:05.520
...and as a master of
the century-old art of Galar Karate.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:09.710
Furthermore, she travels around
visiting dojos all over the world,

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:12.960
battling, refining both herself
and her Pokémon,

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:15.320
in pursuit of even greater strength.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:18.440
Her rank is higher than yours.

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.090
751st, huh?

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:29.790
I’m in the Super Class, too.
I’m 890th.

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:32.380
We’ve won every match
we’ve had so far!

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:34.550
Riolu here has worked
particularly hard!

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:42.770
I can indeed feel a burning fighting spirit from it.
It seems to have been trained well.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.010
I knew you’d be able to tell,
Karate Master!

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:49.500
Hey! I don’t think
you should be so cocky!

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.530
Your opponent is ranked
<i>far</i> above you!

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:56.010
Don’t worry!
Speaking of Fighting-type Gym Leaders,

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:58.570
I beat Corni the other day, remember?

00:07:58.570 --> 00:07:59.290
Corni?

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.780
You know her?

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.620
I have battled her.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.050
Her skills were inadequate.

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:13.510
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.140
There is no need
for me to say more.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.070
Why did you sign up?

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:25.820
Because I wanna get stronger
with my Pokémon!

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:30.030
And if I keep climbing the ranks,
I’ll be able to battle Mr. Dande!

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:33.090
Mr. Dande, is it?

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:37.220
Mr. Dande is every trainer’s goal.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:42.030
I wish to defeat him and become
the undisputed strongest.

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.040
Thus I signed up
for the Championships.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:48.510
<i>I’ll</i> be the strongest!
<i>We</i> will defeat Mr. Dande!

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:50.300
Let us hold nothing back
in our battle!

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:54.630
Don’t panic, Satoshi! Just do
as you always do, and you’ll win, for sure!

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.680
Yeah, I got this!

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:59.420
Pikachu! Riolu!
Let’s do this!

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:12.570
The Pokémon World Championships
has approved this Super Class battle!

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:17.280
The match-up is Contestant Saito
VS Contestant Satoshi.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:20.330
This battle will be a 2v2.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:24.350
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:27.520
3! 2! 1! Go!

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:29.040
Luchabull, go forth!

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.050
You’re up, Kamonegi!
Luchabull, go forth!

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.140
Rotom, who’s that Pokémon?

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:50.510
Luchabull! Wrestling Pokémon!
Fighting/Flying type!

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:54.040
With its wings,
it controls its position in the air!

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:57.150
It overwhelms opponents with quick moves!

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:01.880
Luchabull, huh? Kamonegi,
watch out for its air attacks!

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.080
Battle, start!

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:06.500
Hone Claws!

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.500
Kamonegi,
use Crossroad Kill!

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:17.430
PocketMonsters

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.110
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:23.600
PocketMonsters

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:28.520
Fighting
Riolu
PocketMonsters

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:40.450
It’s got perfect balance!

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:42.830
Karate Chop!

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:51.500
Kamonegi!

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:57.550
Flying Press!

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.130
Kamonegi, grab your leek!

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:06.720
All right!

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:08.790
Good, Kamonegi!

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:12.740
Now! Brutal Swing!

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.610
Spin it around!

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:26.700
Finish it.
Flying Press!

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:36.550
Look up!

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.110
Kamonegi is unable to battle!

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:05.620
No way...

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.000
Return, Kamonegi!

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:16.380
Kamonegi, you did great.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:21.670
It won’t be so easy next time!

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:25.640
It seems she has complete
control over the battle.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:31.770
She called it back?!

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:35.650
Otosupus, go forth!

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.280
Here it comes.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:48.650
Otosupus. Jujitsu Pokémon.
Fighting type.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.660
A body made up of nothing but muscle...

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:54.920
...makes the grappling moves this Pokémon performs
with its tentacles tremendously powerful.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:58.920
That was the Pokémon you were battling
when we came in, right?

00:12:58.920 --> 00:12:59.630
Yes.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:05.540
Neither my Sawamurar nor my Ebiwarar
stood a chance against it.

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:10.930
Riolu, you’ll go?

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:17.610
All right!
Riolu, I choose you!

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:23.610
Pikachu, cheer us on!

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:26.960
My second is Riolu!

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:39.540
Battle, start!

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:40.460
Vacuum Wave!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.850
Charge in!
Detect!

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.020
Infight!

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:01.570
Shadow Clones!

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:12.330
Aqua Break!

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.670
Ward them off, Riolu!

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:33.220
That technique was what defeated
my Sawamurar and Ebiwarar.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.410
Are you okay, Riolu?

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:53.990
I can’t predict its moves.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:55.640
What do we do?

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:07.520
We’ll just have to risk
getting in close to finish it!

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:09.130
Riolu, use Force Palm!

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.850
No! Don’t fight up close!

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.140
Watch out, Riolu!

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:32.300
What can we do?

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:35.140
We can’t get close unless
we deal with those arms.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.780
Satoshi seems to be
having a tough time.

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:46.670
Otosupus lured them into that.

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:57.490
All right, Riolu,
here’s what we’ll do.

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:59.810
Strike under its feet!
Force Palm!

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.020
Oh, my!

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:13.240
Here comes Satoshi’s crazy antics!

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.370
Now!
Use another Force Palm!

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:29.170
Riolu!

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.260
Octolock!

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:37.430
Octolock?!

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.430
His crazy antics didn’t work?!

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:46.420
Is this ground fighting?

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:48.360
He walked right into her trap.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.450
Riolu, hang in there!

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.580
Break free
with Vacuum Wave!

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:03.870
Your technique has too many
wasted movements.

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:12.420
Riolu, your feet!
Kick the floor!

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:30.980
Great work!

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.230
All right!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.740
Hang in there, Riolu!

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:49.540
Aqua Break!

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:52.630
Use Reversal!

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:59.140
It knew Reversal?!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:04.330
A fateful strike that deals more damage
the more damage has been inflicted on the user!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:25.000
Use Octolock again!

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:36.670
Riolu!

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:47.930
Not good!

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:53.190
Forfeit. Otherwise,
I will bring you down.

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:57.390
We won’t lose!
We made it out before!

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:58.610
Hang in there, Riolu!

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:04.450
You leave me no choice.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.660
Aqua Break!

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:19.720
Riolu!

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:27.720
Riolu is unable to battle!

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:32.600
As such, the winner is
Contestant Saito!

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:35.700
I thank you.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:38.040
Are you okay?!

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:42.860
Based on the results of this battle,

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:47.320
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:52.280
Miss Saito won with ease.

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:57.660
Neither Satoshi’s special crazy antics
nor his attempts to outspeed her did him any good.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:20:00.760
Luchabull and Otosupus
are both practically unharmed.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.900
I lost...
completely and utterly.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:15.900
She was really tough, huh, Satoshi?

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:18.150
Return, Otosupus.

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.380
I take my leave.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:28.280
Thank you for allowing us
to battle here.

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:46.220
All right, Go...
Now it’s our turn!

00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:49.430
Who will become your partner?

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:51.800
Defeat me,
and the choice is yours!

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:53.390
Right now?!

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.720
I guess you were
the only winner today.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:08.860
I got Ebiwarar!

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.480
Riolu. Kamonegi.

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:18.130
Sorry. You guys practiced so hard,
but I still lost.

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:25.260
I’ve never had a battle
like that before.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:28.270
But that won’t happen again!

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:30.930
I’ll get my revenge on Miss Saito,
sooner or later!

00:21:32.070 --> 00:21:34.000
The Gym Leader Saito...

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:37.620
...has given Satoshi his first taste of defeat
in the Championships.

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:41.770
He still has a long way to go
to reach the Monarch, Dande!

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:47.320
Let’s play Pokémon Shiritori!

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.530
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)
Let’s play Pokémon Shiritori!

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:50.030
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:50.320
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)
Pokémon Shiritori
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:51.760
Mew!

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:52.510
Warrgle!

00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:53.300
Runpappa!

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:54.070
Pawou!

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:54.810
Ulgamoth!

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:55.600
Strike!

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:56.400
Cresselia!

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:57.110
Amakaji!

00:21:57.110 --> 00:21:57.920
Jirachi!

00:21:57.920 --> 00:21:58.720
Chobomaki!

00:21:58.720 --> 00:21:59.490
Kibago!

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:00.260
Gonbe!

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:01.040
Bayleaf!

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:02.540
Freezer!

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:03.730
Zacian!

